decision: changes-requested

Found six defects, including a remaining part of R1-F5. The repository is unchanged; no attestation was recorded.

Rules applied: POSE review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style and delivery evidence. I inspected the scoped implementation, CI steps, validation registration, spec and regression tests. Package tests and validation rely on the sealed pipeline evidence because this sandbox prohibits writes.

Git’s documented behavior supports the shallow-history, filter-generation and configuration-precedence findings. [Git commit-graph documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-commit-graph), [Git 2.56 implementation](https://github.com/git/git/blob/v2.56.0/commit-graph.c). The partial-clone finding follows Git’s automatic fetching of missing objects. [Partial-clone documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/partial-clone).

