      "file": "pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go",
      "line": 100,
      "summary": "A shallow repository with at least 500 reachable commits receives a fixable rewrite recommendation, but Git refuses both reading and writing commit-graphs while shallow boundaries exist. writeCommitGraph therefore returns success without resolving the finding, violating R2. A read-only probe using --shallow-file with HEAD~499 confirmed a count of 500, is-shallow-repository=true and no Bloom statistics. Git 2.56 commit-graph.c checks commit_graph_compatible for both reads and writes and returns success without writing for shallow history. Detect this condition and provide actionable remediation or explicitly reconcile the requirements; add a shallow-history regression."
