      "summary": "The fix inherits commitGraph.maxNewFilters. With maxNewFilters=0 and no existing filters, --changed-paths computes no new filters, so the command succeeds while the recheck remains next indefinitely. Git documents this setting as the default filter-generation limit; Git 2.56 compute_bloom_filters permits computation only below that limit. R2's promised post-fix ok is therefore not guaranteed. Diagnose the effective generation limit or deliberately override it for this explicit repair, and cover zero and restrictive limits."
    },
    {
      "id": "F11",
      "severity": "low",
      "disposition": "blocker",
      "file": "pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go",
      "line": 80,
      "summary": "An empty HEAD tree above the history threshold returns a successful state with filtersUsed=false before probing or checking disabled reads. doctor.go consequently recommends a rewrite forever, including immediately after a successful fix; disabled-read settings are also omitted. This is possible with an installed, untracked .pose directory and a committed empty tree. R2 has no nonempty-tree exclusion. Handle the absence of a probeable path explicitly and add a regression."
    },
    {
      "id": "F12",
      "severity": "medium",
      "disposition": "blocker",
