      "summary": "The disabled-read diagnosis ignores Git configuration precedence. commitGraph.changedPathsVersion overrides the deprecated commitGraph.readChangedPaths setting. With readChangedPaths=false, changedPathsVersion=1 and a missing graph, this function incorrectly reports reads disabled, removes the automatic repair and asks the user to unset a setting that is ineffective. A read-only trace with both settings confirmed Git actually consulting filters (maybe=1, definitely_not=1141). Resolve the effective version before interpreting the deprecated boolean and test conflicting settings against R3."
    },
    {
      "id": "F13",
      "severity": "medium",
      "disposition": "blocker",
      "file": "pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go",
      "line": 75,
      "summary": "The diagnostic is not guaranteed read-only in a partial clone. Recursive ls-tree, and subsequently the path-history lookup, can encounter promised trees absent locally and cause Git to fetch and store them under the object directory. commitGraphGit uses RawHistoryGit without disabling lazy fetch; gitCommandContext likewise provides no GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH protection. A tree-filtered or sparse partial clone with sufficient history can therefore mutate .git during plain doctor or a fix preview, contrary to the spec's read-only constraint. Disable lazy fetching for diagnostic commands and report unavailable local state; cover missing promised trees without contacting the remote."
    },
    {
      "id": "F14",
      "severity": "medium",
      "disposition": "blocker",
      "file": "pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go",
      "line": 166,
      "summary": "Operational graph-read diagnostics are discarded whenever Git exits successfully. Git can reject a truncated or malformed graph, print an error or warning to stderr, fall back to ordinary object traversal and still complete rev-list/log with exit status zero. This helper then returns no error, and doctor reports next (or ok below the threshold) rather than R3's bounded warn explaining the read failure. Git 2.56 load_commit_graph_one_fd_st rejects undersized files, while prepare_commit_graph permits fallback. Preserve and classify graph-read failures even on successful commands, with a corrupt-graph regression. This leaves R1-F5 partially unresolved."
